<xref rid="B101" ref-type="bibr">Lee et al. (2004)</xref>
</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">CCPA (selective)</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">C57BL/6 mice (renal I/R injury)</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02191; HSP27<sup>q</sup> expression &#x02191; Renal function &#x02193; Pro-inflammatory cytokines &#x02193; Caspase 3 activity</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">HSP27 is an anti-apoptotic molecule as it is associated with an increased resistance to stressful conditions, such as oxidative stress and exposure to toxic drugs A<sub>1</sub>AR- mediated renal protection, anti-inflammatory and anti-apoptotic effects were removed by inhibition of HSP27</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">
